// input: emitted
// NEEDS-ACCEPTANCE: the identified type's body as the printer writes it (the constructors in tag order with their fields); reconcile the two Shape lines below with that syntax.
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not=idr.version --implicit-check-not=idr.entry --implicit-check-not=func.func{{.}}@ --implicit-check-not=idr.erased
// The contract the Idris side emits. The module carries no version, entry
// or entry kind: it holds one program, an op, at the stage before
// defunctionalization, which names its root.
// CHECK-DAG: idr.program @{{[^ ]+}} root(@"$idris-mlir.root") stage(higher) {
// A data type is an identified type whose body declares its constructors,
// in the order of the tags Idris gives them, with their fields.
// CHECK-DAG: {{Prog[.]Shape.*Circle.*i64.*Rect.*i64, i64}}
// Prog's value is a function of no arguments. An erased argument
// is not passed: keep's witness is no argument of the call, and a call
// carries its source location. Under an idr.func, the dialect's ops print
// without their `idr.` prefix.
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func @Prog.result() -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}con {{.*}}Prog.Shape{{.*}} @Rect(%{{[^,]+}} : i64, %{{[^)]+}} : i64)
// CHECK-DAG: call @Prog.keep(%{{[^,)]+}}) : (i64) -> i64 loc("Prog.idr":
// The other functions, in any order: a match on data has one case per
// constructor, its fields the region's arguments; one on an Int matches
// literals. keep and area are total, and keep has one parameter, v.
// countdown recurses on an Int: Idris does not prove that loop
// terminating, so its only fact is its instance. result has no loop of its
// own, so it is total though it calls countdown: whether a call of it may
// diverge is what it reaches (idr-effects); so is the root. A parameter is
// printed with its location, which holds no comma, hence the {{[^,]*}}
// after its type.
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func @Prog.keep(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{[^,]*}}) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func @Prog.area(%{{[^:]+}}: {{.*}}Prog.Shape{{.*}}) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}match %{{[^ ]+}} : {{.*}}Prog.Shape{{.*}} -> (i64) {
// CHECK-DAG: case {{.*}}Circle{{.*}}(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}) {
// CHECK-DAG: case {{.*}}Rect{{.*}}(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}, %{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{.*}}) {
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func @Prog.countdown(%{{[^:]+}}: i64 {{[^,]*}}) -> i64 attributes {instance = #idr.instance<"Prog.countdown"{{[^>]*}}>} {{[{]$}}
// CHECK-DAG: {{(idr\.)?}}match_lit %{{[^ ]+}} : i64 -> (i64) {
// The root, the program on its world, is the one function the program
// names; its symbol is no bare identifier, so it prints quoted.
// CHECK-DAG: idr.func @"$idris-mlir.root"(%{{[^:]+}}: !idr.world {{.*}}) -> {{.*}}PrimIO.IORes{{.*}} attributes {{[{][^}]*}}total
